Description: Fix gclient_paths.py FindInPath to recognize depot-tools hyphen dir
 The MUT (Multiple Upstream Tarball) format extracts depot-tools with
 a hyphen (depot-tools/) instead of underscore (depot_tools/). The
 gclient_paths.py FindInPath() function has a hardcoded check for
 "depot_tools" to avoid infinite recursion when searching PATH for
 tools like gn. When the directory is named "depot-tools", this check
 fails, causing gn.py to find depot-tools/gn (the wrapper) instead
 of /usr/bin/gn, leading to infinite recursion.
 .
 This is the same class of bug fixed in patch 0048 for ninja.py.
 This patch adds "depot-tools" (hyphen) to the check alongside the
 existing "depot_tools" (underscore) check.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-02-16

diff --git a/gclient_paths.py b/gclient_paths.py
index 8ea872f..50c3fee 100644
--- a/gclient_paths.py
+++ b/gclient_paths.py
@@ -195,7 +195,7 @@ def FindInPath(name: str):
     if not env_path:
         return
     for bin_dir in env_path.split(os.pathsep):
-        if bin_dir.rstrip(os.sep).endswith('depot_tools'):
+        if bin_dir.rstrip(os.sep).endswith(('depot_tools', 'depot-tools')):
             # skip depot_tools to avoid calling gn.py infinitely.
             continue
         path = os.path.join(bin_dir, name + GetExeSuffix())
